in @optics/source/ganglion

# @optics/source/ganglion/cartographer — gain medium for the
# cartographer ganglion.
#
# Per docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §10.1, Fate's `cartographer`
# ganglion performs terrain-mapping on holes via
# `@ai/cartographer.map(hole)` (per `boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror`).
# At the optical altitude, cartographer is a 90-port diffractive
# surface (per §10.3, the D²NN identification of Lin et al. 2018);
# the source declaration here carries the active gain that drives the
# surface's transit during the kintsugi loop's ACTIVE pass (per
# §10.2).
#
# === Energy-balance declarations (per spec §3.9) ===
#
#   action       — `refract`. Per §10.3, phase-only diffractive transit.
#   formalism    — `s_matrix`. 90×90 multi-port topology.
#   energy       — `active`.
#   pumping      — `io(channel: ref)`. Per recognition #57.
#   gain_curve   — `ref` at @meta/ast.
#   sat          — `ref` at @meta/ast.
#
# === Why uniform with the other 4 ganglia at v1 ===
#
# Per `shards/optics/source/ganglion.mirror` header: v1 lands all 5
# ganglion sources with uniform shape; per-ganglion specialization
# (e.g., cartographer might prefer a wide flat-top gain curve to
# cover the full mapped territory uniformly) lands when the cascade's
# energy-balance opacity map surfaces the differentiation.
#
# === Recognition #58 Surface B closure ===
#
# One of 5 sources closing recognition #58's v1 gap. See
# `shards/optics/source/ganglion/abyss.mirror` for the full Surface B
# context.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1.7, §3.9, §10.1
#               (cartographer IS mapping ganglion), §10.3, §10.8.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]].
# Related shards: boot/std/fate/connectome.mirror (`cartographer`
#                 variant), boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror
#                 (`@ai/cartographer.map(hole)`),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror.

source @optics/source/ganglion/cartographer {
  action:     refract,
  formalism:  s_matrix,
  energy:     active,
  pumping:    io(channel: ref),
  gain_curve: ref,
  sat:        ref,
  in:         aperture(@optics/aperture/splinter),
  out:        aperture(@optics/aperture/connectome),
}

out @optics/source/ganglion/cartographer
